menu "PhotoPainter firmware frame cache"

config PHOTOPAINTER_ENABLE_CACHE
    bool "Enable the PhotoPainter frame cache partition"
    default y
    help
        Store the last verified frame in the `photocache` data partition so a
        failed fetch keeps the previous screen and a power cut recovers by
        redisplaying it. Requires the partition table to contain a data
        partition with the label below, sized for two slots. Disable this when
        flashing a partition table that has no such partition.

config PHOTOPAINTER_CACHE_PARTITION
    string "Frame cache partition label"
    default "photocache"
    depends on PHOTOPAINTER_ENABLE_CACHE

config PHOTOPAINTER_CACHE_SLOT_SIZE
    int "Frame cache slot size"
    default 262144
    range 196608 1048576
    depends on PHOTOPAINTER_ENABLE_CACHE
    help
        Each A/B slot must fit the 192000-byte packed frame and its metadata.
        Keep this value aligned to the flash erase sector size. The partition
        must be at least twice this size; the shipped table reserves 0x100000,
        which allows growing a slot up to 0x80000.

endmenu
